Two correctness fixes carried by patches/qsa-nvfp4-kv.diff -- zero-filling the
page-aligned strided scratch, and computing gather offsets in int64 -- reproduce
findings from:

  sgl-project/sglang PR #38851
  https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/38851
  "fix(qsa): make the paged sparse-decode gather memory-safe"
  merged 2026-09-11, Apache-2.0

That PR rewrote this same code path but added no FP4 branch, so it does not by
itself enable an FP4 KV cache on the QSA path.
